      "answer_markdown": "Your water bill went up by {F1} from {F2} in April–May to {F3} in June–July. The later period was warmer, so you used more water, adding {F5} to the bill [E2][E1]. Your use also went up by more than the weather explains, which added {F4} [E2][E1][E3]. Water use beyond the weather is up and staying up, and no household note explains it, so this could indicate a leak [E2][E1][E3]. We checked whether the unit price, standing charge, billing period length, estimated readings or one‑off credits played a part, and none of those made a difference.",
